I started playing Nethack (3.4.1) around February or March.  It's taken me
this long to learn how to not make stupid mistakes and retreive the Amulet
of Yendor.  Phew :D!  My notes aren't very good since I didn't expect this
guy to do very well, so forgive the lack of detail.

I took Marchon and his little cat into the dungeon 4 or 5 days ago.  Nothing
to report until level 3 (which also had an altar that I converted) when I
came across a huge hardware shop with 2 bags of tricks, 3 magic lamps (I
already had an oil lamp and these weren't "oil"), a magic marker, a
luckstone (scroll id'd) and a BoH (identified via the "fill it full of
heavy crap" test).  I couldn't afford all of it so I took all of the above
save a 1 lamp and the marker, thinking "I'll be back" (and much later I
was, killed the shopkeeper, mainly to buy protection, and took the marker
and remaining lamp and anything else of value).

I went down the mines to grab some mithril and see what the town had to
offer (which wasn't much), but one level below I came across the grave of a
hapless adventurer, from whom I relieved 2 (cursed) magic lamps, a =oFA, a
=oSD, and +1 rustproof GoP.  Cleared out the mines; meh.  Spent a wish on
speed boots.

Went back up and used the bags of tricks to get Cleaver and more holy water. 
Went to sokoban, cat got killed by some monster I couldn't whack in time. 
Sokoban had a BoH at the end, so I decided to spend a wish on SDSM.

Level 7 had another unfortunate adventurer's final resting gutter from which
I "borrowed" the +2 magicbane, the +6 Vorpal blade, a +5 CoMR, and a +2 t
shirt.  He also had a load of other stuff including Fire Brand (which I
didn't want) and a cursed BoH chock full of wands, scrolls, potions, and
gems (which I "borrowed" as well).  I ditched Cleaver in favour of Vorpal
beheadings and speedy engravings, offed the Troll that killed him (several
times) and went on my merry way.

I doddled down past the rogue level, past the quest level (didn't notice
it), and wound up at Medusa's lair, and killed her.  Somewhere along the
way I picked up a Helm of Brilliance and a silver saber (both of which I
enchanted with zeal), and found a co-aligned temple (with attending
priest!).  Oh, I also stumbled upon Fort Ludios while plundering a magic
memory vault.  Whacked the sissy Croesus, took all his loot in one trip to
my friendly neighborhood Crom-boy (probably developed a hernia), and
managed to get a nice -4 naked AC!  I decided I'd better go find out what
Pelias wanted before continuing.

So I went back and paid attention to the psychic messages this time, went
back home, smacked the coward Thoth Amon (how dare he taunt ME while it's
HIM trying to flee up the stairs!), got some lucky rock and the Bell, and
decided to get rid of some excess baggage (scrolls and wands).  I used up
all my create monster stuff, and polypiled about 200 wands and 50 useless
scrolls.  Didn't get much except for more scrolls, more wands, some usefull
potions, lots of holy water, a "oMB, a "oLS, and crowned.  But I had less
that I started with, so in my own stupid-barbarian way, I won (main goal
was to lighten the load, remember :)?).

Cleaned out the castle.  Never learned how to lower the drawbridge, so I
levitated around back and bonked some heads.  Used the wand for a ring of
conflict, a magic marker, 3 scrolls of charging, and 3 scrolls of genocide. 
I finished the game with several unused wishes and a leftover genocide
scroll (never found extras).

The rest is pretty boring, so I'll try to be quick.  Ate a black dragon on
first level of Gehenomm for disintegration insurance. Killed all the major
demons.  A funny thing happened just before Vlad's tower; I got stuck in a
dead end when a gray unicorn wouldn't cross a magic trap.  I tamed it with
a scroll and took it up to Vlad's tower.  While untrapping the chest with
the "oLS in it, I became stunned and carelessly slaughtered my *pet co
aligned unicorn* in one hit with a Vorpal decapitation.  "Oops" doesn't
begin to describe my embarrasment.  My stupid barbarian couldn't fathom the
luck penalty involved, yet all was cool with Crom by the time we got out of
Gehennom aparently.  Killed the Wizard who didn't give too much trouble
afterwards.  Got The Amulet.  Returned (only got sent back twice!) to the
Dungeon.  Did some final donating/sacrificing/polypiling (only got another
"oLS).  Went to the planes (scrolls and potions got "cancelled" on water)
and ended up on the Astral Plane.

Murphy's Law hit me hard (more like annoying, maybe) here.  Crom's was the
LAST temple I hiked to (on the right).  My angel died after checking out
the center temple, so I put on my ring of conflict and waltzed to the left
(where I was again disappointed).  Whacked Death and Pestilence a few times
each (I thought these guys were scary?).  Got killed by something but
didn't noticed until a few turns had passed ("oLS).  Killed an angel with
Demonbane 2 squares from Crom's alter (easy bonus points), and milked 2
bits from the high priest, and gave Crom his bauble.

Regrets:  This "story" is way longer than I hoped it would be (sorry, and
thanks for reading it all).  Wish that I had've had done this in v3.4.2 so
I could be the first to post an acsension with it, but didn't have dump
patch, and I'm too stupid to figure out how to use screen :).  Wish I
had've taken better notes.

